en you  these are best known for color sports  and architecture but then you have  transcription factors that are also  complicating things and methylation  we have 25 to 34 different malic species  and sadly only a few of them have really  been  leveraged  we have tremendous genetic and  phenotypic diversity apple is wild in  that extent we have self-incompatibility  and inbreeding depression that enforces  reinforces that heterozygosity  and we're clonally propagated that's a  strength because we can fix something  but it's a challenge because there are  many viruses that can be difficult to  detect and once detected can make  commercial commercialization a nightmare  we're also marketed by name which gives  you the ability to  really capitalize on development of the  brand  so you can see  the amazing amount of syntony  the activity of transposable elements  the  methyl methylation that occurs in apple  so what this means is if you find  something a qtl on chromosome 2 you  better also look at chromosome 7 and  chromosome 15 because there are areas of  duplication  so i love transposons somebody else's  twitter account is iheart transposons  but um  this is we have a competition in the lab  to find the most in the field um this  isn't mine so i'm i'm in the second  running but a lot of different  activation of different colors  this russeted chimera was used by one of  my graduate students to be able to  determine that  russeting enhanced the production of  fluoridation  this is an apple that every fruit is  chimeric  gala is similar to that  seedling chimera spur habits also  imposed by a chimera and columnar growth  habit which we feel will have amazing  potential for robotics is also  uh conferred  by activity of transposons  but as again i say nothing is easy we  always used to think that the genetics  of  apple color were pretty straightforward  what these diagrams are showing you is  four different color sports of the same  variety it could be delicious or 